      "output_state": "as-built tensile specimens",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "section": "3.3",
          "quote": "Since sample 8 possesses, simultaneously, the highest density and the highest microhardness level, the process parameter set utilized to fabricate this sample (P = 350 W; v = 2250 mm/s; ET = 0.030 mm; h = 0.09 mm) could be considered as optimum for the AlFeCr alloy investigated. Thefore, these optimized processing conditions were selected to print tensile specimens for further microstructural and mechanical characterization.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "11ecc66d648faaeb:part:001"
        }
      ]
